        "original_id": "648599ad-d585-54aa-879b-80df90e0376f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Works: Louise; Le roi malgré lui; Julien\n- People: Gustave Charpentier; Saint-Pol-Roux; Emmanuel Chabrier; Emile de Najac; Paul Burani\n- Concepts: opera; opéra-comique; sequel\n\nFacts:\n- In 1887, Emmanuel Chabrier created Le roi malgré lui, an opéra-comique in three acts with an original libretto by Emile de Najac and Paul Burani.\n- In 1900, Gustave Charpentier's Louise was the earlier opera to which Julien is a sequel.\n- Louise is a four-act opera described as a \"roman musical\" by Gustave Charpentier, who wrote the original French libretto.\n- Saint-Pol-Roux, a symbolist poet who inspired the surrealists, contributed to the libretto of Louise.\n- Julien is a sequel to Louise and portrays the artistic aspirations of Louise's suitor Julien.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
